{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/195048-agencies","id":195048,"title":"Agencies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-11T15:44:41-07:00","id":195048,"title":"Agencies","content":"Is there a place where people list their Agencies? If not, maybe a few people could throw down some Agencies and Agency ideas here? I'm curious as to how actual players/STs are using these groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:38:38-07:00","id":195130,"title":"","content":"From another thread, here's something I threw together for fun:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Agency: The Technocratic Union</b><br /> <br /> There exists a great Machine that controls reality from behind the scenes. This Machine is not the kindly divine creator so many pray to, but a callous demiurge that regards humanity as little more than playthings. It hides behind an infinite number of masks, burying alien programs in the metaphysical fabric of the city. The Machine has an understanding of physics that enables it to do things most think impossible - you know the old line about 'sufficiently advanced technology' and all that, right? Destroying the Machine isn't possible; it's too deeply embedded in the infrastructure that keeps the world running. The thing is, it isn't impervious to assault. Its tools can be stolen. Its understanding can be gained. The Machine can be <i>used</i>, if one knows where to push. <br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union largely consists of Stigmatic mortals, led by a handful of Integrators and Inquisitors who have banded together.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mission:</b> Use the Machine for good. Guide humanity towards prosperity (and an eventually technological Singularity). Those who comprise the Technocratic Union know the God-Machine exists, and hopes to use the assets it has to build a better future. No small number of transhumanists occupy the Technocratic Union's membership, hoping to use Gadgets to become something <i>better</i> than what they were born as. The council of Unchained that lead the Technocratic Union hope to replace the 'brain' of the God-Machine, guiding it towards their new purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>Resources</b>: Not much, as of yet. The Unchained in charge spend most of their time churning out Gadgets for their agents to use, and have a few boltholes and bits of suborned Infrastructure across [whatever city your chronicle is set in].<br /> <br /> <b>Who's In Charge: </b>The council of Demons who lead the Technocratic Union are referred to as Control by the stigmatics who make up the bulk of membership. They're Integrators and Inquisitors (or more appropriately, Integrator-Inquisitors) with the mother of all goals.<br /> <br /> <b>What's Falling Apart: </b>Plausibility. One ring of demons and a little more than two dozen Stigmatics don't stand much chance of taking down a supernatural entity that spans the globe. They have little to no cash flow and no ready way of replacing those killed by Angels. Control struggles to supply enough Gadgets to give mortal agents a chance in the field. Recruitment is little more than stumbling across Stigmatics in the field and hoping they hop aboard. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T21:40:49-07:00","id":195246,"title":"","content":"<b>Agency: Council for Special Software Acquisitions (UK)</b><br /> <br /> Her Majesty's government is home to hundreds of ministries, sub-ministries, councils, offices and commissions, doing every task imaginable. One enterprising Ring in London decided that in a world were the supernatural is a reality and the world is run by a malignant super-intelligence, someone had to be dealing with all that.<br /> <br /> <i>We not us?</i> they asked.<br /> <br /> After a year of whispering in the ears of MPs, the Ring inserted themselves, two other Rings and some stigmatic allies into public service as the Council for Special Software Acquisitions under the authority the Office of Cyber Security &amp; Information Assurance. Officially, CSSA is responsible for keeping the Government and its ministries informed of firewall, encryption, and anti-malware technologies, make recommendations to Parliament, and obtain cutting edge software relevant to national security.<br /> <br /> Mundane members of the English government have noticed that CSSA is very good at handling matters that no one else will deal with or speak about, so, unofficially, plenty of time and resources are funneled to investigating G-M activity, cryptids, and other supernatural activity. For now, that relationship serves the Agency's interests as they are frequently alerted to information pertinent to their mission.<br /> <br /> Getting to the pub after payday is Sacrosanct.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mission: </b>Investigate G-M activity in the UK. Take appropriate action. Get to the pub.<br /> <br /> <b>Resources: </b>Government offices are not as extravagantly funded as they are on the telly: the computers are ancient, the motorpool decrepit, and the paycheck groans under the cost of living in London. The members of this Agency cope with the discreet use of Embeds and Gadgets: installing Efficiency on the office computers has kept the secretaries from revolting and ensures paperwork does not monopolize the Agency's time. Tempters in the Agency are undertaking a major effort to secure an increased budget.<br /> <br /> The Unchained weathers these inconveniences because of a very important benefit: legitimacy. The CSSA is officially recognized part of the UK Intelligence apparatus, giving it legal mandate to request information from other government branches, carry out investigations, walk the halls of power and speak with anyone it needs to, and receive government funding. It's very nice to go places and do things that would quickly unravel other Covers, <i>and</i> be paid and funded for the trouble.<br /> <br /> As long as someone fills out twenty six forms afterwards.<br /> <br /> In triplicate. Black ink only.<br /> <br /> <b>Who's in Charge:</b> Llywellyn J. Fairfield is the Messenger/Saboteur who works the daily miracle of aligning the interests of three Rings, two dozen human employees, five Stigmatics, a ghoul, and the dizzying array of bureaucrats, politicians and ministers that manage and mismanage UK National Security. Ms. Jacket is a Pyschopomp/ Inquisitor who has become the Agency's defacto Head of Security. It's a job she dislikes, one she doesn't trust anyone else to do, and is very good at.<br /> <br /> <b>What's Falling Apart:</b> CSSA is a victim of its own success. The mundane authorities are using it as a clearing house for Problems No One Wants to Deal With. The Kindred, Forsaken and Awakened communities in London and beyond have identified the CSSA as a potential pawn, threat or opportunity; the possibility of being exposed to one or more of these communities is a nightmare Ms. Jacket now has nightly. One Ring must now be assigned full time to supernatural counterintelligence, a second to the x-files that mortal authorities drop on their doorstep, which one Ring free to pursue Agency missions and investigations. The Rings rotate duties but everyone is trying to cut down on the time spent keeping the enterprise afloat. Some members of the Agency are lobbying to bring the mundane employees into the know under the Official Secrets Act, allowing them to handle sensitive duties and free the time and energy of the Unchained. Others advocate incorporating a fourth and even fifth Ring into the agency. Both of these options are potential security disasters. The mundane employees will demand a raise is the first option is used.<br /> <br /> The local chapter of the Knights of Saint Adrian has started poking around the periphery, putting everyone on edge.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Kindred have inserted a Ghoul named Amanda Park into the Agency. Ms. Park could not be plausibly deflected without alerting the Prince of the London that the CSSA is a supernaturally informed entity. On the other hand, Ms. Park is willing to work odd hours, is good at her job, and makes a <i>very good</i> cup of tea.<br /> <br /> No one is really serious about getting rid of her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":".  grammar 07-16-2014, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T23:05:05-07:00","id":195282,"title":"","content":"That's a really awesome write up that reminds me a lot of the <i>Laundry Files</i>. Kudos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:06:11-07:00","id":195869,"title":"","content":"That's a great write up. Love it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T10:26:05-07:00","id":196959,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Private_intelligence_agency\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Priva...ligence_agency</a> One of these could be perfect for an Agency. It spends much of it's time doing regular intelligence stuff for governments or other corporations, but watches the GM as much as possible. Heck, maybe the company is just infiltrated by the characters ring, a paranormal private intelligence company, looking into ghosts, demons and other supernatural stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T22:05:24-07:00","id":216469,"title":"","content":"<b>Agency: Four LearClover Importing LLC</b>.<br /> <br /> In a tiny alley way on a second story floor on Dodge island, port of Miami there is a cramped, sweaty office with the unassuming sign \u201cImport/Export.\u201d If you say the right words (this week it\u2019s a set of hand signals from the 1965 world series), the burly man at the reception desk, Mr. Coat, will show you past four doors, one Iron, one wood, on silver, one of black glass. In the back of the office is the air-conditioned, luxurious appointed, and surprisingly large office of Ms. Coin, over looking the gorgeous waters of Miami.<br /> \u201cIf you need it, I can get it,\u201d she says with a smile.<br /> <br /> Ms. Coin discovered the Exploit Rip the the Gates several years ago while trying to master Trick of the Light. After accidentally casting herself into the Hedge, she found her way to the local Goblin Market, embarked on a shopping spree and bought her way to earth. She declared that that was the best trip ever, and that she wanted to go again.<br /> <br /> The Four LearClover Importing specializes in traveling into the realms beyond and obtaining valuables for trade. The agency coffers are growing, both in cash, supernatural commodities, contracts and favors.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mission:</b> Import goods/ services from places off earth: the Hedge, the Shadow, the Underworld and the Astral Realms. The Agency also specializes in transporting willing supernatural creatures.<br /> Prices are, of course, what the client can bear.<br /> <br /> <b>Resources: </b>Currently, the Agency\u2019s most important asset is the alliance it has with the local Changeling Autumn Court. Ms. Coin has spent years building a stable relationship that profits both parties. The Agency expressly forbids soul pacts to make themselves more palpable to the Changelings.<br /> The doors in the Agency are Exploited gadgets that serve as aetheric beacons, lighthouses for Agent conducting missions in the far realms, giving them an edge in finding their way back home.<br /> <br /> <b>Who\u2019s in Charge: </b>Ms. Coin has founded the Agency and sets its agenda. Mr. Tree is a recognized export on supernatural security, or would be, if the Unchained did things like recognize each other for expertise.<br /> <br /> <b>Whats Falling Apart: </b>Ms. Coin is an expert businesswoman and entrepreneur, but \u2018Courageous\u2019 is a Very Bad vice to have.<br /> The Agency incurred the wrath a True Fey thwarting a kidnapping attempt against the local Autumn King. The Barony of Fracture is plotting revenge once he (it?) has a grasp of what the Unchained are.<br /> The the door to Hedge is a Lambda gadget that allows someone to exit the Hedge, a feature that was not possible with the original Exploit. If the Autumn Court knew, they could explain what a horrible idea this is.<br /> Finally, yesterday an executive of the Deva Corporation walked into the agency headquarters with a too-wide smile on his face and said <i>\u201cI think we can help each other. You don\u2019t get to say \u2018no\u2019.&quot; </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}